{
 "name": "Lagoa house: rain look (Rain colour 2026-11-14)",
 "notes": "Every day colour name used here -> its rainy colour. A colourful tropical downpour, not a grey filter: each colour keeps its day hue and at least its day chroma (greens 24% richer and deeper, glossy highlights kept bright), lightness drops about 10-16%, and a soft blue-teal sky light (OKLab hue 232) cools the true neutrals and casts faintly on the rest (looks.rain_formula). Outdoor = the full shift; indoor = the same shift at half strength. These are look colours (exact formula values, like the night twins), not pack palette entries. 'sheen' = a wet highlight on paving (rain colour lifted 42% towards rn_sky0); 'window_light' = the cool light through the glass indoors; 'extra' = rain-only colours (the soft blue-violet overcast sky rn_sky0-2, rn_glint for drops and glints, rn_mist).",
